course/modules/M/M5/L07.html:414:              <p>The quotient for the pair is \((\cos 0.995 - \cos 1)/(1 - 0.995) = 0.8401167\ldots\), which matches the printed maximum to six decimal places. The quotient is an average of \(\sin t\) over \([0.995, 1]\) (Assumptions 1 and 2(c)). By Assumption 2(a), \(\sin t < \sin 1\) for every \(t < 1\), so this average is strictly less than \(\sin 1\), because the interval has width \(0.005 > 0\) and ends at \(1\). The printed maximum is below \(\sin 1\) by \(\sin 1-0.8401167257\ldots=0.0013542591\ldots\), computed from unrounded values. The quotients for the pairs \((1-h,1)\) tend to \(\sin 1\) as \(h \to 0\), as Problem R3 shows.</p>
